  "text": "Classic Neapolitan ice cream is a traditional Italian dessert that features three distinct flavors: vanilla, chocolate, and strawberry. It's often served as a single scoop with a mix of the three flavors, and sometimes comes in a cone. Here's a simple recipe to make your own Neapolitan ice cream at home:\n\n---\n\n### **Classic Neapolitan Ice Cream Recipe**\n\n#### **Ingredients** (Makes about 1 quart / 4 cups)\n\n##### **For the Vanilla Base:**\n- 2 cups whole milk\n- 1 cup heavy cream\n- 3/4 cup sugar\n- 1 tbsp vanilla extract\n- 1/4 tsp salt\n\n##### **For the Chocolate Swirl:**\n- 1/2 cup unsweetened cocoa powder\n- 1/4 cup butter\n- 1/4 cup sugar\n- 1/2 cup heavy cream\n- 1/4 tsp salt\n- 1 tbsp vanilla extract\n\n##### **For the Strawberry Swirl:**\n- 1 (14 oz) can crushed pineapple, drained\n- 1/4 cup sugar (adjust to taste)\n- 1 tbsp lemon juice\n- 1 tbsp cornstarch (optional, for thickening)\n\n---\n\n### **Instructions**\n\n#### 1. **Make the Vanilla Base:**\n- In a medium saucepan, combine the milk, cream, sugar, salt, and vanilla extract.\n- Heat over medium heat, stirring until the sugar dissolves.\n- Remove from heat and let cool to room temperature.\n- Churn in an ice cream maker according to the manufacturer\u2019s instructions until it reaches a soft-serve consistency.\n\n#### 2. **Prepare the Chocolate Swirl:**\n- In a small saucepan, melt the butter and cocoa powder over low heat.\n- Add the sugar, cream, salt, and vanilla. Stir until well combined and smooth.\n- Cool the mixture in the refrigerator for 1\u20132 hours, or until it\u2019s thick and ready to swirl into the vanilla base.\n\n#### 3. **Prepare the Strawberry Swirl:**\n- In a bowl, mix the crushed pineapple, sugar, and lemon juice.\n- If using cornstarch, mix it with a little water and stir into the pineapple mixture to thicken it slightly.\n- Let the mixture chill in the refrigerator for 1 hour.\n\n#### 4. **Assemble the Ice Cream:**\n- Once the vanilla base is ready (soft-serve consistency), flavor it with the cooled chocolate and strawberry mixtures.\n- Chill the ice cream in the freezer for at least 2\u20133 hours, or until it\u2019s firm enough to scoop.\n- Serve in cones or cups, or freeze for longer storage.\n\n---\n\n### **Tips:**\n- For a more authentic flavor, use high-quality vanilla beans or pure vanilla extract.\n- You can adjust the sweetness to your taste by adding more or less sugar.\n- If making in a batch, mix the swirls into the base with a spoon just before freezing for a more distinct three-flavor experience.\n\nEnjoy your homemade Neapolitan ice cream! \ud83c\udf66",
